IMPORT prelude

-- Home Team Corps Act 2017 (Singapore) -- who is a member (s 2), who may join and which Corps (s 9), discharge and dismissal of
-- cadets (s 10), summary discipline of cadets and its punishments (ss 11, 12), boards of inquiry into officers (s 13),
-- compensation for death or injury on duty (s 14), the weapons-law exemption (s 15), and the Commandant's term (s 6(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation
-- (the deposit's page furniture reads "version in force from 1/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/HTCA2017.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 31 of 2023 wef 01/12/2025, to the
-- definition of "permanent resident" in s 2.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0134 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to (here, mainly a school student
-- in the NPCC or NCDCC, and the teachers and volunteers who run them); no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to
-- the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: establishment and organisation (ss 3, 4), the Council's composition and
-- delegation (s 5), appointment of Commandants and officers beyond what s 2 needs (ss 6(1), (2), (4), 7), secondment (s 8),
-- general and routine orders (s 16), the regulation-making power (s 17) and the saving and transitional provisions (s 18). No
-- regulations or orders made under the Act were retrieved, so what a cadet's period of service, the allowances, or the amount
-- of compensation are, is not known here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Home Team Corps Act 2017 -- cadets and officers`

DECLARE Corps IS ONE OF
    `the National Police Cadet Corps`
    `the National Civil Defence Cadet Corps`

§§ `2 -- who is a member`

-- s 2: "member" means "an officer of, or a cadet enrolled in," either Corps, "and includes an individual undergoing an officer
-- cadet course". "officer" means "an individual appointed as an officer, an honorary officer or an honorary instructor under
-- section 7(1), (2) or (3)". So an honorary instructor -- s 7(3), a volunteer who is not a cadet or officer -- is an "officer" and
-- therefore a "member". A police or civil defence officer seconded under s 8 is not, by these words, an officer of the Corps
-- unless also appointed under s 7 (an inference: s 8 seconds them "for ... service in" the Corps but does not appoint them).
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a cadet`
    `a teacher appointed as an officer`
    `an honorary officer`
    `an honorary instructor`
    `a trainee on an officer cadet course`
    `a police officer seconded to the NPCC`
    `a parent helping at an event`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a member` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `a police officer seconded to the NPCC` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a parent helping at an event` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `9 -- who may join, and which Corps`

-- s 9(1): "a citizen of Singapore or a permanent resident is eligible to be enrolled as a cadet or appointed as an officer in one
-- of the following Corps, but not both". (2): "The Minister may in special cases approve the enrolment as a cadet, or the
-- appointment as an officer, of an individual who is neither a citizen of Singapore nor a permanent resident."
-- Whether the "not both" bar binds a s 9(2) approval is not said; it is applied here to everyone (an inference).
-- The Act sets no age; age is left to regulations (s 17(2)(d)).
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Minister's special approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is already in the other Corps` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is eligible` IF
        (    `the applicant`'s `is a citizen`
         OR  `the applicant`'s `is a permanent resident`
         OR  `the applicant`'s `has the Minister's special approval`)
    AND (NOT `the applicant`'s `is already in the other Corps`)

§§ `10 -- discharge and dismissal of cadets`

-- s 10(1): a cadet "is discharged from service in that Corps when the cadet has completed the period of service for which the
-- cadet was enrolled". The period itself is not in the Act.
GIVEN `months served` IS A NUMBER, `months enrolled for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cadet is discharged` IF
    `months served` AT LEAST `months enrolled for`

-- s 10(2): a cadet "may be dismissed by the competent authority -- (a) on the recommendation of the cadet's officer-in-charge; and
-- (b) where the cadet is a student of a school, with the concurrence of the principal of the school". (3): the competent authority
-- is the Commandant of the cadet's own Corps. ("school" means a school to which the Education Act 1957 applies, s 2.)
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Commandant of the NPCC`
    `the Commandant of the NCDCC`
    `the officer-in-charge`
    `the school principal`

GIVEN `the corps` IS A Corps
GIVETH A Authority
`the competent authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the corps`
    WHEN `the National Police Cadet Corps` THEN `the Commandant of the NPCC`
    WHEN `the National Civil Defence Cadet Corps` THEN `the Commandant of the NCDCC`

GIVEN `the corps` IS A Corps,
      `who dismisses` IS A Authority,
      `the officer-in-charge recommended it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the cadet is a school student` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principal concurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dismissal is valid` IF
        `who dismisses` EQUALS `the competent authority` `the corps`
    AND `the officer-in-charge recommended it`
    AND ((NOT `the cadet is a school student`) OR `the principal concurred`)

§§ `11 -- when a cadet is dealt with summarily`

-- s 11: a cadet who "(a) in such manner as to show wilful defiance of authority, disobeys any lawful command ...; or (b)
-- contravenes any general or routine order ... or regulation ..., being an order or regulation known to the cadet or that the
-- cadet might reasonably be expected to know, must be dealt with summarily by the cadet's officer-in-charge".
-- This is a disciplinary matter, not an offence: the Act creates no offence and no fine or imprisonment.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `disobeyed a lawful command` IS A BOOLEAN
    `showed wilful defiance of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contravened an order or regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `might reasonably be expected to know of it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cadet must be dealt with summarily` IF
        (`the conduct`'s `disobeyed a lawful command` AND `the conduct`'s `showed wilful defiance of authority`)
    OR  (    `the conduct`'s `contravened an order or regulation`
         AND (`the conduct`'s `knew of it` OR `the conduct`'s `might reasonably be expected to know of it`))

§§ `12 -- summary punishments of a cadet`

-- s 12: "if a finding of guilt is recorded", the officer-in-charge may impose one or more of "(a) reprimand; (b) where the cadet
-- holds a rank, reduction in rank; (c) suspension of membership ... for a period not exceeding 3 months". Dismissal is not on
-- the list; it goes through s 10(2).
DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `a reprimand`
    `reduction in rank`
    `suspension of membership`
    `dismissal`
    `a fine`
    `detention`

GIVEN `the punishment` IS A Punishment,
      `guilt was recorded` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the cadet holds a rank` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `suspension months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer-in-charge may impose it` IF
    `guilt was recorded`
    AND CONSIDER `the punishment`
        WHEN `a reprimand` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `reduction in rank` THEN `the cadet holds a rank`
        WHEN `suspension of membership` THEN `suspension months` AT MOST 3
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `13 -- boards of inquiry into officers`

-- s 13(3): if the board "is of the opinion that an officer is guilty of a breach", it "must recommend to the Commandant ... which
-- of the following punishments or combination of them should be imposed: (a) reprimand; (b) reduction in rank; (c) dismissal".
-- The board recommends; the Act does not say who then imposes it (presumably the Commandant -- an inference).
GIVEN `the punishment` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a board of inquiry may recommend it` IF
    CONSIDER `the punishment`
    WHEN `a reprimand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reduction in rank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dismissal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 13(2)(a): the Chairperson is, for an NPCC officer, "a police officer not below the rank of Assistant Superintendent of Police
-- or an officer of the National Police Cadet Corps not below the rank of Assistant Superintendent"; for an NCDCC officer, "an
-- officer of the Singapore Civil Defence Force not below the rank of Captain of Civil Defence or an officer of the National Civil
-- Defence Cadet Corps not below the rank of Captain". (b): "at least 2 other individuals, one of whom must be nominated by a
-- Permanent Secretary to the Ministry of Education".
DECLARE Chair IS ONE OF
    `a police officer of ASP rank or above`
    `a police officer below ASP rank`
    `an NPCC officer of Assistant Superintendent rank or above`
    `an SCDF officer of Captain rank or above`
    `an NCDCC officer of Captain rank or above`
    `a school principal`

GIVEN `the corps` IS A Corps, `the chair` IS A Chair
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chair is qualified` IF
    CONSIDER `the corps`
    WHEN `the National Police Cadet Corps` THEN
        CONSIDER `the chair`
        WHEN `a police officer of ASP rank or above` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an NPCC officer of Assistant Superintendent rank or above` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `the National Civil Defence Cadet Corps` THEN
        CONSIDER `the chair`
        WHEN `an SCDF officer of Captain rank or above` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an NCDCC officer of Captain rank or above` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the corps` IS A Corps,
      `the chair` IS A Chair,
      `other members` IS A NUMBER,
      `one is nominated by MOE` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board is properly constituted` IF
        `the chair is qualified` `the corps` `the chair`
    AND `other members` AT LEAST 2
    AND `one is nominated by MOE`

§§ `14 -- compensation for death or injury on duty`

-- s 14: "It is lawful for the Minister to compensate, in accordance with regulations ..., any member or the member's dependants
-- for the member's death or personal injury arising out of or in the execution of the member's duty and that is attributable
-- SOLELY to the discharge of the member's duty." It is a power ("lawful for the Minister"), not an entitlement.
GIVEN `the role` IS A Role,
      `arose out of or in the execution of duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `attributable solely to the discharge of duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may compensate` IF
        `the person is a member` `the role`
    AND `arose out of or in the execution of duty`
    AND `attributable solely to the discharge of duty`

§§ `15 -- exemption from the weapons laws`

-- s 15: "Nothing in the Arms Offences Act 1973 and the Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958 applies to
-- members while on parade or in the course of their duty."
GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `on parade or on duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the weapons laws are disapplied` IF
    `the person is a member` `the role` AND `on parade or on duty`

§§ `6(3) -- the Commandant's term`

-- s 6(3): a Commandant "holds office for a period specified by the Minister (which in no case exceeds 3 years) and is eligible for
-- re-appointment on completion of that period".
GIVEN `years specified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commandant's term is lawful` IF
    `years specified` GREATER THAN 0 AND `years specified` AT MOST 3
